05-4|drk.final:
The NextBillion Tracking SDKs have no class called a "location tracking manager". You initialize the `AssetTracking` SDK and receive location updates through `AssetTrackingCallback`. On Android, the closest match by name is `LocationPermissionsManager`, which only handles permissions.

The examples below are condensed from the official docs, and I haven't compiled them. On both platforms, the flow is initialize → register callback → create and bind an asset → start tracking.

## Android (Kotlin)

**Add these permissions to `AndroidManifest.xml`:**

```xml
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION" />
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" />
<!-- API level >= 29 -->
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION" />
```

**Initialize the SDK and listen for updates:**

```kotlin
class GetAssetCallback : AppCompatActivity(), AssetTrackingCallBack {
    private var permissionsManager: LocationPermissionsManager? = null
    private var assetId = ""

    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)

        initialize("PUT YOUR API KEY HERE")
        assetTrackingAddCallback(this)
        createAndBindAsset()
    }

    override fun onDestroy() {
        super.onDestroy()
        assetTrackingRemoveCallback(this)
    }

    // Callbacks
    override fun onLocationSuccess(location: Location) {
        Log.d("Tracking", "${location.latitude}, ${location.longitude}")
    }

    override fun onLocationFailure(exception: Exception) {
        Log.e("Tracking", exception.message ?: "Location error")
    }

    override fun onTrackingStart(assetId: String) {
        Log.d("Tracking", "Started: $assetId")
    }

    override fun onTrackingStop(assetId: String, trackingDisableType: TrackingDisableType) {
        Log.d("Tracking", "Stopped: $assetId")
    }

    // Create and bind the asset
    private fun createAndBindAsset() {
        val profile = AssetProfile.Builder()
            .setCustomId(UUID.randomUUID().toString())
            .setName("testName")
            .setDescription("testDescription")
            .setAttributes(mapOf("attribute 1" to "test 1"))
            .build()

        createNewAsset(profile, object : AssetApiCallback<AssetCreationResponse> {
            override fun onSuccess(result: AssetCreationResponse) {
                assetId = result.data.id
                bindAsset(assetId, object : AssetApiCallback<Unit> {
                    override fun onSuccess(result: Unit) {
                        checkPermissionsAndStartTracking()
                    }
                    override fun onFailure(exception: Exception) {
                        Log.e("Tracking", "Bind failed: ${exception.message}")
                    }
                })
            }
            override fun onFailure(exception: Exception) {
                Log.e("Tracking", "Create failed: ${exception.message}")
            }
        })
    }

    // Check permissions and start tracking
    @SuppressLint("MissingPermission")
    private fun checkPermissionsAndStartTracking() {
        if (LocationPermissionsManager.areAllLocationPermissionGranted(this)) {
            assetTrackingStart()
            return
        }
        permissionsManager = LocationPermissionsManager(object : LocationPermissionsListener {
            override fun onExplanationNeeded(permissionsToExplain: List<String>?) {
                // Explain why location access is needed
            }

            override fun onPermissionResult(granted: Boolean) {
                if (!granted) return
                if (LocationPermissionsManager.isBackgroundLocationPermissionGranted(this@GetAssetCallback)) {
                    assetTrackingStart()
                } else {
                    permissionsManager?.requestBackgroundLocationPermissions(this@GetAssetCallback)
                }
            }
        })
        permissionsManager?.requestLocationPermissions(this)
    }

    override fun onRequestPermissionsResult(
        requestCode: Int,
        permissions: Array<String>,
        grantResults: IntArray
    ) {
        super.onRequestPermissionsResult(requestCode, permissions, grantResults)
        permissionsManager?.onRequestPermissionsResult(requestCode, permissions, grantResults)
    }
}
```

## iOS (Swift)

**Add these keys to `Info.plist`:**

```xml
<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
<string>[Your explanation here]</string>
<key>NSLocationAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
<string>[Your explanation here]</string>
<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
<array>
  <string>location</string>
</array>
```

**Initialize the SDK and listen for updates:**

```swift
class GetAssetCallbackViewController: UIViewController, AssetTrackingCallback {

    override func viewDidLoad() {
        super.viewDidLoad()
        AssetTracking.shared.initialize(apiKey: "YOUR_API_KEY")
        AssetTracking.shared.delegate = self
        createAndBindAsset()
    }

    func createAndBindAsset() {
        let profile = AssetProfile(
            customId: UUID().uuidString.lowercased(),
            assetDescription: "testDescription",
            name: "testName",
            attributes: ["attribute 1": "test 1"]
        )

        AssetTracking.shared.createAsset(assetProfile: profile) { response in
            let assetId = response.data.id
            AssetTracking.shared.bindAsset(assetId: assetId) { _ in
                AssetTracking.shared.startTracking()
            } errorHandler: { error in
                print("Bind failed: \(error.localizedDescription)")
            }
        } errorHandler: { error in
            print("Create failed: \(error.localizedDescription)")
        }
    }

    // AssetTrackingCallback
    func onLocationSuccess(location: CLLocation) {
        print("\(location.coordinate.latitude), \(location.coordinate.longitude)")
    }

    func onLocationFailure(error: Error) {
        print("Location error: \(error.localizedDescription)")
    }

    func onLocationServiceOff() {
        // Prompt the user to enable Location Services
    }

    func onTrackingStart(assetId: String) {
        print("Started: \(assetId)")
    }

    func onTrackingStop(assetId: String, trackingDisableType: NBAssetTracking.TrackingDisableType) {
        print("Stopped: \(assetId)")
    }
}
```

## Callback reference

| Event | Android | iOS |
|---|---|---|
| New location | `onLocationSuccess(location: Location)` | `onLocationSuccess(location: CLLocation)` |
| Error | `onLocationFailure(exception: Exception)` | `onLocationFailure(error: Error)` |
| Tracking started | `onTrackingStart(assetId)` | `onTrackingStart(assetId:)` |
| Tracking stopped | `onTrackingStop(assetId, trackingDisableType)` | `onTrackingStop(assetId:trackingDisableType:)` |
| Location services off | No callback | `onLocationServiceOff()` |
| Register | `assetTrackingAddCallback(this)` | `AssetTracking.shared.delegate = self` |
| Unregister | `assetTrackingRemoveCallback(this)` | No method documented |

## Things to check

- **Changes from the docs:** the official examples start tracking from a button tap. I start it automatically after a successful bind, so tracking begins without user input. I also replaced the UI updates with logging.
- **Android interface name:** the docs spell it two ways, `AssetTrackingCallBack` in the example and `AssetTrackingCallback` in the guide. Use whichever your SDK version exposes.
- **Android `onTrackingStop`:** the guide also lists a single-argument `onTrackingStop(assetId)`, but the example only overrides the two-argument version. If the compiler complains, check the interface in your SDK version.
- **Android location services:** the official example also checks `LocationPermissionsManager.isLocationServiceEnabled(this)` and shows a dialog if they're off. I left that out, so add it for production.
- **API keys:** the examples use a placeholder, so don't hardcode a real key in a production app.

## Sources

**Android**
- [Get AssetTrackingCallback example](https://docs.nextbillion.ai/tracking/android-tracking-sdk/examples/get-assettracking-callback)
- [Asset Tracking Callback](https://docs.nextbillion.ai/tracking/android-tracking-sdk/asset-tracking-callback)
- [Location Manager](https://docs.nextbillion.ai/tracking/android-tracking-sdk/location-manager)

**iOS**
- [Get AssetTrackingCallback example](https://docs.nextbillion.ai/tracking/ios-tracking-sdk/examples/get-assettracking-callback)
- [Asset Tracking Callback](https://docs.nextbillion.ai/tracking/ios-tracking-sdk/asset-tracking-callback)
- [Location Manager and Collection](https://docs.nextbillion.ai/tracking/ios-tracking-sdk/location-manager-and-collection)

