In the Flutter Navigation SDK, you avoid toll roads by passing `SupportedAvoid.toll` in the `avoid` list of `RouteRequestParams`, then fetching the route as usual.

```dart
RouteRequestParams requestParams = RouteRequestParams(
  origin: origin,
  destination: dest,
  avoid: [SupportedAvoid.toll],
  // To avoid more than one feature:
  // avoid: [SupportedAvoid.toll, SupportedAvoid.ferry],
);

NBNavigation.fetchRoute(requestParams, (routes, error) async {
  // Use the returned routes, or handle the error
});
```

The `avoid` line appears commented out in the docs' sample as an optional parameter, so I've enabled it here. The `fetchRoute` call comes from the docs' route-fetching example, but I haven't compiled or run this code.

**Sources:**
- [Flutter Navigation SDK: Usage, Fetch routes](https://docs.nextbillion.ai/routing/flutter-navigation-sdk/usage#fetch-routes): the `RouteRequestParams` sample
- [Launch Embedded NavigationView](https://docs.nextbillion.ai/routing/flutter-navigation-sdk/examples/launch-embedded-navigationview#fetching-route-with-routerequestparams): route options, including avoiding tolls or ferries
- [Fetch Route and Launch Navigation](https://docs.nextbillion.ai/routing/flutter-navigation-sdk/examples/fetch-route-and-launch-navigation#fetch-route-with-routerequestparams): the `NBNavigation.fetchRoute` flow
- [Directions API: Avoid Tolls & Highways](https://docs.nextbillion.ai/routing/directions-api/examples/avoid-tolls-and-highways): the top match outside the Flutter docs, which I haven't opened

