# Customize Route Line Style (Flutter Navigation SDK)

This guide shows how to draw a route with `NavNextBillionMap` and style it with `RouteLineProperties`. You pass the properties in when creating `NavNextBillionMap` in the `_onStyleLoaded` callback.

## `RouteLineProperties` attributes

| Property | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `routeDefaultColor` | `Color` | Default color of the main route line |
| `alternativeRouteDefaultColor` | `Color` | Default color of alternative route lines |
| `routeShieldColor` | `Color` | Shield icon color for the route |
| `alternativeRouteShieldColor` | `Color` | Shield icon color for alternative routes |
| `routeScale` | `double` | Scale factor for the route line width |
| `alternativeRouteScale` | `double` | Scale factor for the alternative route line width |
| `originMarkerName` | `String` | Asset image name of the origin marker |
| `destinationMarkerName` | `String` | Asset image name of the destination marker |
| `durationSymbolPrimaryBackgroundColor` | `Color` | Background color of the primary route's duration symbol |
| `durationSymbolAlternativeBackgroundColor` | `Color` | Background color of the alternative route's duration symbol |
| `durationSymbolPrimaryTextStyle` | `TextStyle` | Text style of the primary route's duration symbol |
| `durationSymbolAlternativeTextStyle` | `TextStyle` | Text style of the alternative routes' duration symbols |

## Apply the style

```dart
void _onStyleLoaded() async {
  if (controller != null) {
    var routeLineStyle = const RouteLineProperties(
        routeDefaultColor: Color(0xFFE97F2F),
        routeScale: 1.0,
        alternativeRouteScale: 1.0,
        routeShieldColor: Color(0xFF54E910),
        durationSymbolPrimaryBackgroundColor: Color(0xFFE97F2F));
    navNextBillionMap = await NavNextBillionMap.create(controller!,
        routeLineProperties: routeLineStyle);
  }
}
```

## Fetch and draw the route

```dart
void _fetchRoute() async {
  RouteRequestParams requestParams = RouteRequestParams(
    origin: origin,
    destination: dest,
    mode: ValidModes.car,
  );

  DirectionsRouteResponse response =
      await NBNavigation.fetchRoute(requestParams);
  List<DirectionsRoute> routeData = response.directionsRoutes;
  if (routeData.isNotEmpty) {
    setState(() {
      routes = routeData;
    });
    drawRoutes(routeData);
  }
}

Future<void> drawRoutes(List<DirectionsRoute> routes) async {
  navNextBillionMap.clearRoute();
  navNextBillionMap.drawRoute(routes);
}
```

## Start navigation

```dart
void _startNavigation() {
  if (routes.isEmpty) return;
  NavigationLauncherConfig config =
      NavigationLauncherConfig(route: routes.first, routes: routes);
  config.locationLayerRenderMode = LocationLayerRenderMode.gps;
  config.shouldSimulateRoute = true;
  config.themeMode = NavigationThemeMode.system;
  config.useCustomNavigationStyle = false;
  NBNavigation.startNavigation(config);
}
```

The example uses the `nb_maps_flutter` and `nb_navigation_flutter` packages. You'll need the required permissions and API keys set up to use these services.

The snippets above are shortened. The doc's full widget also includes the `NBMap` setup and the "Fetch Route" and "Start Navigation" buttons.

## Links

- **Android snapshot:** https://static.nextbillion.io/docs-next/docs/navigation/flutter/examples/customize-route-line-style-1.webp
- **iOS snapshot:** https://static.nextbillion.io/docs-next/docs/navigation/flutter/examples/customize-route-line-style-2.webp
- **Full example source:** https://github.com/nextbillion-ai/nb-navigation-flutter/blob/main/example/lib/route_line_style.dart
- **Documentation:** https://docs.nextbillion.ai/routing/flutter-navigation-sdk/examples/customize-route-line-style

